        "historyItemId": "Awz1Z63m3sRcIOGafUg4"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/chia-seeds/voice/voice-v1-blocks/03-fats.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-carbs",
      "index": 3,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "carbs",
      "text": "42.1 grams of carbs. Fibre is massive at 34.4 grams, so this is much more about fullness and digestion than fast carbs. Sugar is 0 grams, and glycemic index is 1, so the carb profile stays very steady. The weak point is starch at 0 grams, meaning this is not a steady-starch fuel.",
      "textSha256": "2201fb037846c88fa0b47f488c0f16c04734ac2f3e35887d6de0d5578873224b",
      "characterCount": 280,
      "byteLength": 338591,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/chia-seeds/voice-v1-blocks/04-carbs.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "Qg7xj6v0FIhJEDgc2DCW",
        "historyItemId": "LuyFvvKinZGb9PJF2P4g"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/chia-seeds/voice/voice-v1-blocks/04-carbs.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-proteins",
      "index": 4,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "proteins",
      "text": "16.5 grams of protein. That is decent for a seed, but it sits just under the 18 grams useful-protein gate. Essential amino acids score is 0 out of 9 after that gate, so protein helps here but does not become the main reason to use chia.",
      "textSha256": "45c3bcb5564fd1162110b3f0927c424223636c9ea787d02e0af51db8f31dda0b",
      "characterCount": 236,
      "byteLength": 326470,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/chia-seeds/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "aoRbmTqMwREDuhvPP3Ri",
        "historyItemId": "GtahO8Ti7VgcdmHFqfmK"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/chia-seeds/voice/voice-v1-blocks/05-proteins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-vitamins",
      "index": 5,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "vitamins",
      "text": "Vitamins are low overall. Vitamin E is only 3% daily value, so there is not much vitamin support here. For seeds, the better story is fats and minerals, not vitamins.",
      "textSha256": "5602bfe12f8e8b34ad6f98e4ece5deaec648d5fdc98c6971b401fcb1a8711ffc",
      "characterCount": 166,
      "byteLength": 194813,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/chia-seeds/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "1meiLAWhyHcXqAaKn37C",
        "historyItemId": "242djl1k0qtfNmSztFr2"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/chia-seeds/voice/voice-v1-blocks/06-vitamins.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-minerals",
      "index": 6,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "minerals",
      "text": "Magnesium is 80% daily value, the clear mineral strength. Calcium is 49% daily value, iron is 43% daily value, and zinc is 42% daily value, so the backup mineral profile is broad too. For seeds, this is a real strength.",
      "textSha256": "bdce31d0b7774659f7effa2f3112059a0d85a76418643f353fef80438b87ac91",
      "characterCount": 219,
      "byteLength": 304318,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/chia-seeds/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "gtlk4axzOInHyLVx1S1f",
        "historyItemId": "4Kg3a1Micmyig8pDrGy2"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/chia-seeds/voice/voice-v1-blocks/07-minerals.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-pros",
      "index": 7,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "pros",
      "text": "Pros first: fuller texture helps real meals. The gel can make yogurt, oats, and smoothies feel more filling. ALA omega-3 is the headline fat. That is the food-specific reason chia stands out among seeds. Easy to boost meals invisibly. A small spoonful can disappear into everyday meals.",
      "textSha256": "d2562acebae58fb41d216404abb24f060f35bb9509a4ac870383396c721e47da",
      "characterCount": 286,
      "byteLength": 350293,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/chia-seeds/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "Kp3eQYXAITtbTeDpjw0P",
        "historyItemId": "vetxW1iVVb6MTOQUwjcf"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/chia-seeds/voice/voice-v1-blocks/08-pros.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-cons",
      "index": 8,
      "kind": "section",
      "sectionKey": "cons",
      "text": "Cons next: works best with enough fluid. Dry chia is awkward unless it is soaked or mixed properly. Phytates add an absorption caveat. The mineral numbers are high, but absorption is not automatic. Gel texture and digestion can be divisive. The same thing that helps satiety can put some people off.",
      "textSha256": "587960668e152d1fab2b7f0622560b6bcc0ef2789b03b1dad6b6c70a03a59059",
      "characterCount": 299,
      "byteLength": 351965,
      "audioFile": "docs/audio/episodes/chia-seeds/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3",
      "elevenLabs": {
        "requestId": "ShcBWk1n0dmYgD6zIoiF",
        "historyItemId": "PJ49gHExLMMHhcSLZnrB"
      },
      "productionAudioFile": "production/episodes/chia-seeds/voice/voice-v1-blocks/09-cons.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-closing_summary",
      "index": 9,
      "kind": "closing_summary",
      "sectionKey": null,
      "text": "Best bits are omega 3, fibre, and minerals. Weak spots are vitamins, gated protein quality, and texture tolerance. Best for heart health, digestion, and meal-boosting because the fibre is huge, the fat profile is unusual, and a small amount can upgrade simple foods.",
      "textSha256": "110fdbfdadfb4bedc25cf9d68d243188d8d2a66575b3d4ae0b39962db2fe5eb1",
      "characterCount": 266,
      "byteLength": 318528,
